  "content": {
    "id": "p29-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Find the condition for each GP to have a limiting sum, then find that limiting sum.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p29-q11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$7+7x+7x^2+\\cdots$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-1<x<1$; $S_\\infty=\\dfrac{7}{1-x}$.",
          "worked": "$r=x$. For a limiting sum, $|r|<1$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}|x|&<1\\\\-1&<x<1\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}S_\\infty&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\\\S_\\infty&=\\frac{7}{1-x}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$2x+6x^2+18x^3+\\cdots$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\dfrac13<x<\\dfrac13$; $S_\\infty=\\dfrac{2x}{1-3x}$.",
          "worked": "$r=3x$. For a limiting sum, $|r|<1$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}|3x|&<1\\\\-1&<3x<1\\\\-\\frac13&<x<\\frac13\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}S_\\infty&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\\\S_\\infty&=\\frac{2x}{1-3x}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$1+(x-1)+(x-1)^2+\\cdots$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0<x<2$; $S_\\infty=\\dfrac{1}{2-x}$.",
          "worked": "$r=x-1$. For a limiting sum, $|r|<1$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}|x-1|&<1\\\\-1&<x-1<1\\\\0&<x<2\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}S_\\infty&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\\\S_\\infty&=\\frac{1}{1-(x-1)}\\\\S_\\infty&=\\frac{1}{2-x}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q11-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$1+(1+x)+(1+x)^2+\\cdots$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-2<x<0$; $S_\\infty=-\\dfrac1x$.",
          "worked": "$r=1+x$. For a limiting sum, $|r|<1$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}|1+x|&<1\\\\-1&<1+x<1\\\\-2&<x<0\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}S_\\infty&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\\\S_\\infty&=\\frac{1}{1-(1+x)}\\\\S_\\infty&=-\\frac1x\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      }
    ]
  },
